From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Xun2202 <98207886+Xun2202@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 07:36:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ui: rebuild text-only refractive glass navigation and hide on
 fast return swipes

Shared with the other Harmony Tachiyomi fork. Use one background-only AGSL refraction layer on API 33+, a thinner Haze backdrop and directional rim/press light; keep text sharp with contrast-aware Difference ink. Remove per-tab lens, icons and selection frame; retain centered labels, counters, semantics and drag-to-select. Give left/right/bottom one total safe gap and match reported screen corner curvature when possible. User clarified fast throws in either direction must hide: classify from instantaneous and tracked movement as well as release velocity, while preserving slow reveal, pressed touch latch and boundary/refresh guards. Cover the actual panorama scrollable, bidirectional flings, text centering and native Skia shader pixels.
